{#
  The dictionary-entry create form.

  **`locale` is enabled here and disabled on the edit page**, which is a real behavioural
  difference and not a rendering one: `DictionaryEntryForm` declares the element
  `'disabled' => false` with a `@todo how can I block this without disabling it?`, and
  dictionary/create.phtml then re-enables it explicitly. A moderator picks the language when
  creating an entry and cannot change it afterwards. Reproduced with `setAttribute`, in the
  template, because that is where the original does it — the form class is shared with the
  edit surface and must not be mutated for one of them from a factory.

  No submit here: the field partial renders its own, on both surfaces.

  The create page is the edit page with a different heading, a different action and no
  record — which is exactly what laminas says too: create.phtml and edit.phtml are separate
  view scripts that include the same fields-partial.phtml. So this template **extends its
  edit twin** and overrides only what differs. What that inherits is the page's assets and
  its inline scripts, which on laminas come from the shared partial rather than from either
  view script, so inheriting them is the faithful arrangement rather than a shortcut.
#}
{% extends 'books/dictionary-entry-edit.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate('Create new dictionary entry') }}</h1>

{% do form.get('locale').setAttribute('disabled', false) %}
{{ form_open(form, form_action) }}
{{ include('books/_dictionary-entry-fields.html.twig') }}
{{ form_close() }}
{% endblock %}
